st sales now we had a tie  here at 20 and it gave them both third  place and then it skipped fourth place  and went to fifth place and that's how  the basic rank function works  so if we duplicate it  and we edit our copy  and we're going to make this one  rank dense  you know what let's do rank modified  second  okay  and we bring on rank modified  let's have this happen in order so sum  of sales then rank then rank modified  now you can see  it's similar to rank first second but  then it skips third and goes to fourth  and then fifth so over here it gave them  buyer number when there was a tie and  over here it gave them the lower number  when there was a tie  so if you could remember that  rank gives them the higher number and  rank modified gives them the lower  number that will be helpful  for your interview  now we're going to take a look at rank  dense  rank dense apply  and rank dense doesn't skip a number so  it goes one two three four and it  condenses  the ranking  without any skipping any numbers  and now let's  do our last one  which is going to be  rank unique  okay  and with rank unique it refuses to give  to  the same rank  and how it determines when there is a  tie  is it will look at the dimension  that's in the visualization and do  whichever one comes first in ascii so it  goes one two and these are a tie and  since capital b comes before  lowercase c  then it's doing b first then c  then a  so in your interview it would be really  impressive to talk about the different  versions of ranks and how they all work  question 23 how can you embed a web page  in a dashboard so we're just going to  build this and then explain it so i have  here my map by sales and we're going to  build a dashboard  we'll bring on first we'll change our  layout so i can fill up the screen  then let's bring on my map  and i've added the state name and the  sales on the map here  for  an embedded web page you can grab it  from the objects section the web page  and then you 